      Metasploit Framework - Open-source penetration testing and exploitation framework
        Initial exploitation procedure: Select and configure exploit modules, customize payloads (msfvenom), set up multi-handler listener, execute exploit against target, and establish initial access through reverse shell or meterpreter session
        Network reconnaissance procedure: Use auxiliary modules for port scanning, service enumeration, vulnerability scanning, and credential harvesting against target networks
        Privilege escalation procedure: Utilize local exploit modules, run post-exploitation scripts, exploit Windows vulnerabilities (e.g., EternalBlue), and leverage captured credentials for privilege elevation
        Persistence establishment procedure: Install backdoors, create scheduled tasks, modify registry keys, and deploy web shells using meterpreter or shell sessions
        Lateral movement procedure: Use PSExec modules, WMI commands, or SMB exploits to move between systems, and establish multiple concurrent sessions across the network
        Credential harvesting procedure: Dump password hashes using hashdump modules, extract credentials from memory with Mimikatz integration, capture network authentication attempts, and crack or reuse harvested credentials
        Data exfiltration procedure: Search and collect sensitive files, compress data, establish covert channels using DNS/ICMP, and exfiltrate through encrypted meterpreter sessions
        Resource script automation procedure: Create custom resource scripts (.rc files) for automated exploitation, configure multi-stage attack sequences, and schedule automated tasks
        Evasion procedure: Encode payloads using multiple iterations, bypass antivirus using encrypted communications, implement sleep timers, and use process migration to avoid detection
        Pivoting procedure: Set up SOCKS proxy, configure port forwarding rules, establish pivot listeners, and route traffic through compromised hosts to reach segmented networks
