        Network protocol reverse engineering: Extract protocol structures, analyze packet handling, rebuild communication flows, document protocol specifications
        Custom loader development: Implement file format parsing, handle non-standard executables, map segments correctly, resolve relocations
        Exploit development workflow: Identify vulnerability points, analyze security mechanisms, develop proof-of-concept code, test exploitation paths
        Obfuscated code analysis workflow: Handle control flow flattening, decode string encryption, reconstruct obfuscated logic, document deobfuscation steps
        Memory forensics integration: Analyze memory dumps, reconstruct runtime structures, trace dynamic allocations, correlate with static analysis
        Mobile binary analysis procedure: Handle ARM/ARM64 binaries, analyze iOS/Android protections, reverse native libraries, understand runtime interactions
        Kernel driver analysis workflow: Map driver structures, analyze device I/O, trace interrupt handlers, understand kernel interactions
        Multi-architecture analysis: Compare implementations across architectures, identify equivalent functions, document platform differences
        Virtual machine bytecode analysis: Reverse custom VM implementations, decode bytecode operations, reconstruct original logic
        Code similarity analysis: Identify similar functions across binaries, track code reuse, generate similarity signatures
        Time-critical analysis procedure: Quick triage of binaries, identify key functionality, prioritize analysis targets, document critical findings
