      Subfinder - Subdomain discovery tool
        Basic subdomain enumeration: Execute "subfinder -d domain.com" to discover subdomains using default providers
        Configure multiple API keys: Set up API keys for providers (VirusTotal, SecurityTrails, etc.) in ~/.config/subfinder/provider-config.yaml
        Silent enumeration with output to file: Run "subfinder -d domain.com -silent -o output.txt" for clean output
        Recursive enumeration: Use "subfinder -d domain.com -recursive" to discover subdomains of discovered subdomains
        Multi-threaded enumeration: Employ "subfinder -d domain.com -t 100" to increase concurrent threads
        Filter active subdomains: Combine with httpx using "subfinder -d domain.com | httpx -silent"
        Custom resolvers: Use "subfinder -d domain.com -r resolvers.txt" with specific DNS resolvers
        All sources enumeration: Execute "subfinder -d domain.com -all" to use all available sources
        Exclude specific sources: Run "subfinder -d domain.com -exclude censys,shodan" to skip certain providers
        Multiple domain enumeration: Use "subfinder -dL domains.txt" to enumerate subdomains for multiple domains
        JSON output format: Use "subfinder -d domain.com -oJ" for structured JSON output format
        Host IP resolution: Execute "subfinder -d domain.com -ip" to include host IP addresses in results
        Time-based enumeration: Run "subfinder -d domain.com -timeout 30" to set custom timeout
        Active verification: Use "subfinder -d domain.com -active" to verify subdomain resolution
        Custom ports scanning: Combine with naabu using "subfinder -d domain.com | naabu -p 80,443,8080"
        Exclude specific subdomains: Execute "subfinder -d domain.com -exclude-ip" to omit IP addresses
        Source selection: Run "subfinder -d domain.com -sources censys,shodan" to use specific sources
        CSV output format: Use "subfinder -d domain.com -oC" for CSV formatted output
        Rate limiting: Execute "subfinder -d domain.com -rate-limit 10" to control requests per second
        Proxy usage: Run "subfinder -d domain.com -proxy http://proxy.example.com" for proxied requests
        Wildcard filtering: Use "subfinder -d domain.com -nW" to exclude wildcard subdomains
        Historical enumeration: Combine with waybackurls using "subfinder -d domain.com | waybackurls"
        Automation script: Create bash script to run subfinder with multiple domains and automated reporting
        CI/CD integration: Configure subfinder in GitLab/GitHub workflows for automated reconnaissance
        Custom regex filtering: Pipe output through grep to filter specific patterns "subfinder -d domain.com | grep -E 'pattern'"
        DNS record types: Execute "subfinder -d domain.com -r resolvers.txt -t A,AAAA,CNAME" for specific records
        Real-time monitoring: Set up cron job to periodically run subfinder and alert on new subdomains
        Cloud integration: Deploy subfinder on cloud instance for distributed enumeration
        Custom configuration file: Use "subfinder -d domain.com -config custom-config.yaml" for specific settings
        Database integration: Pipe results to SQLite/MongoDB for historical tracking and analysis
