      Wapiti - Web application vulnerability scanner
        Basic web application scan: Execute Wapiti with default modules against target URL, generate HTML report of findings
        SQL injection scan: Configure and run Wapiti with --module=sql focus to detect SQL injection vulnerabilities
        XSS detection: Use --module=xss parameter to scan for cross-site scripting vulnerabilities in forms and parameters
        File inclusion scan: Enable file inclusion module (--module=file) to detect LFI/RFI vulnerabilities
        Command injection testing: Run command injection module (--module=exec) to identify OS command injection flaws
        Authentication bypass: Use --auth-method and related parameters to test authentication mechanisms
        Cookie manipulation: Enable cookie handling and session analysis for security testing
        Custom payload injection: Configure custom attack payloads using --endpoint-params for targeted testing
        Crawling configuration: Set up detailed crawling parameters (scope, depth, excluded URLs) for thorough scanning
        Automated exploitation: Chain detected vulnerabilities with payload generation for proof-of-concept attacks
        Proxy configuration: Set up Wapiti behind a proxy/SOCKS server for anonymous scanning
        Custom headers injection: Add specific HTTP headers to requests for testing security controls
        Performance tuning: Configure parallel connections and timeouts for optimized scanning
        Network authentication: Use --http-credentials for scanning protected web applications
        Advanced reporting: Generate machine-readable outputs (JSON/XML) for integration with other tools
        Certificate handling: Configure SSL/TLS options for scanning HTTPS sites with invalid certificates
        Scan resume capability: Use --resume-crawl and --resume-attack to continue interrupted scans
        Module chaining: Create custom module combinations for targeted vulnerability assessment
        Error handling configuration: Set up custom error detection patterns for accurate vulnerability identification
        Scope control: Define strict domain boundaries using --scope options to prevent unauthorized scanning
        Scan scheduling: Configure cron jobs or scheduled tasks for automated periodic scanning
        Color output configuration: Use --color parameter to customize console output for better readability
        Verbose logging: Enable detailed logging with -v parameter for debugging and analysis
        Database export: Export scan results to SQLite database for custom analysis
