        Conduct targeted subnet scanning with specific ports: masscan -p22,80,443,3389 192.168.0.0/16 --rate=1000
        Execute banner grabbing scan: masscan -p80,443 10.0.0.0/8 --banners --source-ip [spoofed_ip]
        Use exclude file to avoid scanning specific IPs: masscan -p0-65535 192.168.0.0/24 --excludefile exclude.txt
        Perform SYN scan with randomized target selection: masscan --rand-source -p21,22,23,25,80,443 172.16.0.0/12
        Output results in JSON format: masscan -p1-65535 10.0.0.0/8 -oJ scan_results.json
        Configure scan timing and packet rate: masscan -p80,443 192.168.1.0/24 --rate=100 --wait=0
        Scan specific port ranges: masscan --ports 0-1024 172.16.0.0/16 --rate=5000
        Use multiple source IP addresses: masscan -p80,443 10.0.0.0/8 --source-ip 192.168.1.1,192.168.1.2
        Perform adaptive scan with retry options: masscan -p22,80,443 192.168.0.0/16 --retries=2 --rate=1000
        Perform stealth scanning with reduced packet rate: masscan -p80,443 192.168.0.0/16 --rate=10 --wait=30
        Use custom TCP flags for scan: masscan -p80,443 10.0.0.0/8 --tcp-flags SYN,ACK,RST,FIN
        Save results in XML format for tool integration: masscan -p1-1024 172.16.0.0/12 -oX scan.xml --max-rate 1000
        Configure scan with specific TTL value: masscan -p22,80,443 192.168.0.0/24 --ttl 127
        Perform ping sweep using ICMP echo: masscan --ping 10.0.0.0/8 --rate=10000
        Execute scan with custom MAC address: masscan -p80,443 192.168.1.0/24 --router-mac 00:11:22:33:44:55
        Use custom payload for scanning: masscan -p80 172.16.0.0/12 --data "HTTP/1.1\r\n\r\n"
        Configure scan with specific source port: masscan -p80,443 10.0.0.0/8 --source-port 53
        Perform scan with IPv6 targets: masscan -p80,443 2001:db8::/32 --rate=1000
        Use rotating source ports for evasion: masscan -p22,80,443 192.168.0.0/16 --source-port 40000-60000
        Generate offline list for later scanning: masscan -p80,443 10.0.0.0/8 --generate-list > targets.txt
        Resume interrupted scan: masscan -p0-65535 192.168.0.0/16 --resume paused.conf
        Segment large networks for distributed scanning: masscan -p22,80,443 192.168.0.0/16 --shard 1/10
        Perform scan with specific seed for reproducibility: masscan -p80,443 10.0.0.0/8 --seed 123456
        Use custom HTTP User-Agent: masscan -p80,443 172.16.0.0/12 --http-user-agent "Mozilla/5.0"
        Configure scan with specific network interface: masscan -p80,443 192.168.1.0/24 --interface eth0
        Output results in list format for grep: masscan -p1-65535 10.0.0.0/8 -oL results.txt
        Perform scan with specific top ports: masscan --top-ports 100 192.168.0.0/16
        Use connection timeout settings: masscan -p80,443 172.16.0.0/12 --connection-timeout 10
        Configure scan with specific adapter IP: masscan -p22,80,443 10.0.0.0/8 --adapter-ip 192.168.1.10
        Perform scan with DNS resolution: masscan -p80,443 example.com --resolvers 8.8.8.8
        Execute scan with specific IP protocol: masscan --ip-protocol 1 10.0.0.0/8 --rate=1000
        Configure scan with custom hello string: masscan -p443 192.168.0.0/16 --hello-string "SSL"
        Use append mode for output files: masscan -p22,80,443 172.16.0.0/12 -oJ results.json --append-output
        Perform scan with specific MTU size: masscan -p80,443 10.0.0.0/8 --mtu 1500
        Configure scan with specific network range file: masscan -p80,443 --includefile ranges.txt
        Use rotation of multiple configuration files: masscan -p1-65535 --conf-rotate configs/*.conf
        Execute scan with custom TCP options: masscan -p80,443 192.168.0.0/24 --tcp-option-mss 1460
        Perform scan with specific timestamp: masscan -p80,443 10.0.0.0/8 --timestamp relative
        Configure scan with router MAC discovery: masscan -p22,80,443 172.16.0.0/12 --router-mac-lookup
