      Nikto - Web server scanner
        Basic web server scanning: Execute nikto -h target_host to perform comprehensive scan of web server vulnerabilities, misconfigurations, and outdated software
        Scan multiple ports: Use nikto -h target_host -p port1,port2,port3 to scan specific ports for web services
        Tuning scan types: Implement nikto -Tuning x where x is numbers 1-9 to focus on specific vulnerability categories
        Authentication scanning: Configure nikto -id username:password to test with credentials against protected resources
        SSL/TLS scanning: Execute nikto -ssl to force SSL/TLS scanning of the target
        Custom output generation: Use nikto -Format htm,csv,txt -o output_file to generate reports in multiple formats
        Proxy implementation: Configure nikto -useproxy http://proxy:port to route scans through proxy server
        Evasion techniques: Apply nikto -evasion technique_number to use various IDS evasion methods
        Plugin selection: Execute nikto -Plugins plugin_name to run specific vulnerability checks
        Manual cookie injection: Use nikto -Cookies cookie_string to test with specific session cookies
        Virtual host scanning: Use nikto -vhost hostname to scan virtual hosts on the target server
        Custom database updates: Execute nikto -update to update vulnerability database before scanning
        Bandwidth throttling: Implement nikto -delay N to add delays between requests to reduce network load
        CGI scanning: Configure nikto -CGI to focus specifically on CGI script vulnerabilities
        Custom user agent: Use nikto -useragent "custom string" to specify different browser identities
        Mutation techniques: Apply nikto -mutate 1,2,3 to perform mutation-based testing of parameters
        Server version checks: Execute nikto -Version to enumerate server versions and technologies
        Follow redirects: Use nikto -followredirects to automatically follow HTTP redirects during scanning
        Debug mode scanning: Implement nikto -Debug to capture detailed scanning information
        Save resume state: Configure nikto -Save file to enable scan resumption capabilities
        HTTP method testing: Use nikto -Method POST,PUT,DELETE to test specific HTTP methods
        Compliance checking: Execute nikto -Single "plugin_id" to test for specific compliance requirements
        No SSL validation: Implement nikto -nossl to skip SSL certificate validation
        Custom timeout settings: Configure nikto -timeout N to set custom timeouts for requests
        Enhanced logging: Use nikto -Display V to show verbose output during scanning
        Integration with other tools: Pipe nikto output to other tools using -Format csv
        Custom port ranges: Execute nikto -ports range to scan non-standard port ranges
        Root directory specification: Use nikto -root /custom/path to specify alternate root path
        Host header manipulation: Configure nikto -vhost "host_header" for virtual host testing
        Response filtering: Implement nikto -404code xxx to handle custom 404 responses
