        Use custom headers and cookies for authenticated scanning (e.g., 'gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt -H "Cookie: session=123"')
        Enumerate virtual hosts (e.g., 'gobuster vhost -u http://target.com -w vhost-wordlist.txt')
        Use proxy settings for anonymous scanning (e.g., 'gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt -p http://proxy:port')
        Implement custom status code filtering (e.g., 'gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt -s "200,301,302,401"')
        Perform fuzzing with pattern matching (e.g., 'gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt -p pattern')
        Use wildcard detection to eliminate false positives (e.g., 'gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt --wildcard')
        Configure output formats for reporting (e.g., 'gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt -o output.txt')
        Implement rate limiting to avoid detection (e.g., 'gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt -z --delay 100ms')
        Use custom username/password for basic authentication (e.g., 'gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt -U user -P pass')
        Perform case-insensitive searching (e.g., 'gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt -i')
        Expand media file discovery (e.g., 'gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt -x jpg,png,gif,pdf')
        Configure custom User-Agent strings (e.g., 'gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt -a "CustomAgent/1.0"')
        Use multiple wordlists concatenation (e.g., 'cat wordlist1.txt wordlist2.txt > combined.txt && gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w combined.txt')
        Implement blacklisting of specific response sizes (e.g., 'gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt -b "1234,4321"')
        Follow redirects for thorough enumeration (e.g., 'gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt -r')
        Customize timeout settings for slow responses (e.g., 'gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt --timeout 10s')
        Use expanded mode for detailed output (e.g., 'gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt -e')
        Chain Gobuster with other tools (e.g., pipe output to Nmap: 'gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt | grep "Status: 200" | cut -d " " -f1 | nmap -iL -')
        Use TLS/SSL configuration options (e.g., 'gobuster dir -u https://target.com -w wordlist.txt -k --tls-skip-verify')
        Implement custom DNS resolution (e.g., 'gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt --resolver 8.8.8.8:53')
        Perform recursive directory scanning (e.g., 'gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt -r -d 3')
        Use pattern matching with regular expressions (e.g., 'gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt --pattern-match "^admin"')
        Apply custom HTTP methods (e.g., 'gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt -m POST,PUT')
        Implement negative status code filtering (e.g., 'gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt -b "404,500"')
        Use random user agents rotation (e.g., script to rotate User-Agents with Gobuster)
