      Aquatone - Domain flyover tool
        Use Aquatone with subfinder/amass output to discover and screenshot all subdomains: cat domains.txt | aquatone -out ./aquatone
        Configure custom scan settings with increased threads and longer timeouts: aquatone -threads 50 -scan-timeout 3000
        Perform header analysis on discovered hosts: aquatone -collect-headers
        Generate HTML report with visual site clustering: aquatone -out ./report -chrome-path /path/to/chrome
        Chain with nmap output for targeted visual reconnaissance: nmap -p80,443 -oX scan.xml | aquatone
        Utilize custom browser headers and cookies for authenticated scanning: aquatone -cookie "session=xyz" -header "User-Agent: Custom"
        Integrate with cloud enumeration tools for targeted screenshots: aquatone -ports xlarge
        Export results to JSON format for automated analysis: aquatone -out results -json
        Perform targeted screenshots of specific URL paths: echo "example.com/admin" | aquatone -path-only
        Use proxy chains for stealth scanning: aquatone -proxy http://127.0.0.1:8080
        Implement automated daily domain monitoring: cron + aquatone + diff previous results
        Chain with Burp Suite for selective scanning: burp-to-aquatone.sh | aquatone
        Perform selective technology fingerprinting: aquatone -tags wordpress,joomla
        Use custom Chrome flags for evasion: aquatone -chrome-options "--headless,--disable-gpu"
        Generate side-by-side comparison reports of historical scans: aquatone-diff.py
        Filter and screenshot specific HTTP response codes: aquatone -filter-codes 200,403,500
        Integrate with DNS zone transfer results: dig axfr domain.com | aquatone
        Customize screenshot resolution and quality: aquatone -resolution 1920,1080 -quality high
        Set up distributed scanning using multiple agents: aquatone-cluster
        Create targeted scans based on web technology fingerprints: aquatone -wappalyzer
        Perform time-based scanning for detecting dynamic content: aquatone -interval 24h
        Use custom JavaScript injection for enhanced page interaction: aquatone -js "document.querySelector('.popup').click()"
        Implement geolocation-based scanning using VPN rotation: aquatone-geo-scan
        Create filtered scans based on SSL/TLS versions: aquatone -ssl-version tls1.2,tls1.3
        Generate visual sitemaps from screenshot results: aquatone-sitemap
        Perform mobile device emulation scanning: aquatone -user-agent "iPhone" -viewport mobile
        Set up alert triggers for visual changes: aquatone-alert
        Chain with content discovery tools: ffuf output | aquatone
        Execute authenticated scans using session files: aquatone -session-file auth.json
        Implement custom screenshot triggers based on DOM events: aquatone -wait-for ".loaded"
      Subfinder - Subdomain discovery tool
        Execute basic subdomain enumeration using default sources: `subfinder -d domain.com`
        Utilize multiple API keys for enhanced discovery: Configure ~/.config/subfinder/provider-config.yaml with API keys from sources like Shodan, SecurityTrails, and VirusTotal
        Perform recursive subdomain enumeration: `subfinder -d domain.com -recursive`
        Filter active subdomains using probe: `subfinder -d domain.com -active`
