        Use custom resolvers for DNS resolution: `subfinder -d domain.com -r resolvers.txt`
        Silent enumeration with specific sources: `subfinder -d domain.com -silent -sources shodan,censys,virustotal`
        Exclude specific sources: `subfinder -d domain.com -exclude sources.txt`
        Use with other tools: Pipe output to httpx/nuclei for further reconnaissance
        Enumerate multiple domains simultaneously: `subfinder -dL domains.txt`
        Implement rate limiting for stealth: `subfinder -d domain.com -rl 10`
        Use custom timeout settings: `subfinder -d domain.com -t 10`
        Filter subdomains by regex patterns: `subfinder -d domain.com | grep -E "dev|staging|test"`
        Maximize enumeration with all sources: `subfinder -d domain.com -all`
        Configure proxy for anonymous scanning: `subfinder -d domain.com -proxy http://proxy:port`
        Use with alterations and permutations: `subfinder -d domain.com -all | altdns -i - -o altered.txt`
        Implement in automation scripts: Create bash/python scripts for scheduled scanning
        Combine with wildcard filtering: `subfinder -d domain.com | dnsx -resolver 8.8.8.8 -wildcard`
        Use with domain bruteforcing: Combine output with tools like massdns for comprehensive enumeration
