        Check for exposed configuration files and backups (wpscan --url [target] --enumerate cb) to find security misconfigurations
        Perform comprehensive scan with vulnerability verification (wpscan --url [target] --api-token [token] -e vp,vt,tt,cb,dbe --plugins-version-detection aggressive)
        Perform authenticated scan with password hash (wpscan --url [target] --wp-content-dir [custom_path] --wp-plugins-dir [custom_path] --cookie [auth_cookie])
        Generate detailed vulnerability reports in JSON format (wpscan --url [target] --format json --output scan_report.json)
        Scan multiple targets using input file (wpscan --url-list [targets.txt] --random-user-agent --ignore-main-redirect)
        Execute custom API queries for vulnerability database (wpscan --url [target] --api-token [token] --custom-api-check [plugin_name])
        Perform targeted scanning of specific WordPress components (wpscan --url [target] --include-content [themes,plugins,timthumbs])
        Bypass WAF/IPS detection using custom headers (wpscan --url [target] --headers [headers.txt] --random-user-agent)
        Test for XML-RPC vulnerabilities (wpscan --url [target] --enumerate x --plugins-version-detection mixed)
        Scan for specific CVEs in WordPress core (wpscan --url [target] --api-token [token] --vulnerability-refs [CVE-XXXX-YYYY])
        Perform distributed scanning using proxy lists (wpscan --url [target] --proxy [proxy_list.txt] --proxy-auth [credentials])
        Execute custom WordPress API endpoint enumeration (wpscan --url [target] --enumerate ap --api-requests [custom_endpoints.txt])
        Perform WordPress security hardening compliance checks (wpscan --url [target] --enumerate dbe,cb --wp-version-all --check-wp-config)
        Execute time-based scanning with automated rescans (wpscan --url [target] --detection-mode mixed --batch --force --schedule [cron_expression])
        Integrate WPScan with continuous integration pipelines (wpscan --url [target] --format cli-no-color --exit-on-vulnerable)
        Conduct custom password policy assessment (wpscan --url [target] --password-policy-check --enumerate u --rules [policy_file.txt])
        Perform targeted scanning based on WordPress API responses (wpscan --url [target] --enumerate ap --api-response-analysis [custom_rules.txt])
        Execute comparative scans across multiple WordPress versions (wpscan --url [target] --compare-versions --api-token [token])
        Generate compliance reports for security frameworks (wpscan --url [target] --format json --output [report.json] --compliance [standard])
        Perform staged scanning with progressive intensity (wpscan --url [target] --staged-scan [config.yml] --progressive-timeout)
        Execute custom plugin vulnerability assessment (wpscan --url [target] --custom-plugin-checks [checks.rb] --api-token [token])
        Implement rate-limited scanning for high-availability targets (wpscan --url [target] --rate-limit [requests/second] --availability-check)
