        Execute targeted enumeration focusing on specific record types: dnsenum [domain] --type A,MX,NS,SOA
        Use DNSenum with custom DNS servers: dnsenum [domain] --server [DNS_server_IP] --threads 10
        Perform enumeration with IPv6 support enabled: dnsenum [domain] --ipv6
        Execute DNSenum with private WHOIS server: dnsenum [domain] --whois --private
        Use DNSenum with custom TCP/UDP ports: dnsenum [domain] --port [port_number]
        Integrate DNSenum output with other tools using script mode: dnsenum [domain] --script [script_file]
        Perform selective enumeration excluding specific record types: dnsenum [domain] --exclude A,AAAA
        Execute DNSenum with custom user-agent strings: dnsenum [domain] --useragent "Custom String"
        Use DNSenum with proxy support for anonymous scanning: dnsenum [domain] --proxy [proxy_address]
        Implement rate limiting to avoid detection: dnsenum [domain] --delay [seconds]
        Execute targeted enumeration for specific subdomains: dnsenum [domain] -s [subdomain_list]
        Combine DNSenum with dictionary mutation for advanced subdomain discovery: dnsenum [domain] -f [wordlist] --mutate
        Execute DNSenum in debug mode for detailed operation analysis: dnsenum [domain] --debug
        Use DNSenum with custom wildcard resolution handling: dnsenum [domain] --wildcard
        Perform targeted enumeration with specific DNS record class: dnsenum [domain] --class IN
        Execute DNSenum with custom timeout for each query type: dnsenum [domain] --timeout-mx 5 --timeout-axfr 10
        Use DNSenum with maximum subdomain depth specification: dnsenum [domain] --depth 3
        Implement DNS cache snooping techniques: dnsenum [domain] --cache-snoop
        Execute DNSenum with custom TTL monitoring: dnsenum [domain] --ttl-track
        Use DNSenum with DNSSEC validation: dnsenum [domain] --dnssec
        Perform enumeration with specific DNS protocol version: dnsenum [domain] --dns-version 1.1
        Execute DNSenum with custom regular expressions for filtering: dnsenum [domain] --regex "[pattern]"
        Perform passive DNS enumeration using historical data: dnsenum [domain] --passive
        Use DNSenum with custom certificate transparency log queries: dnsenum [domain] --ct-logs
        Implement custom DNS record handling with scripted responses: dnsenum [domain] --script-response
        Execute DNSenum with specific DNS transport encryption: dnsenum [domain] --dns-over-tls
        Use DNSenum for DNS pinning vulnerability testing: dnsenum [domain] --dns-pinning
        Perform enumeration with custom EDNS options: dnsenum [domain] --edns
