      PsExec - Sysinternals tool for remote command execution and process control
        Execute remote commands using PsExec with explicit credentials: psexec \\target -u domain\username -p password cmd
        Deploy and run executables remotely: psexec \\target -c application.exe
        Launch interactive command shell on remote system: psexec \\target -s -i cmd.exe
        Execute commands with SYSTEM privileges: psexec -s -i cmd.exe
        Install and run services on remote systems: psexec \\target -i -d service.exe
        Copy and execute files across multiple systems: psexec @hostlist.txt -c script.bat
        Run PowerShell commands remotely: psexec \\target powershell.exe -command "command"
        Establish persistent access through service creation: psexec \\target -i -d -s backdoor.exe
        Execute commands without requiring SMB file share: psexec -r notepad \\target cmd
        Perform network enumeration through command execution: psexec \\target net view /domain
        Create scheduled tasks on remote systems: psexec \\target schtasks /create /tn "TaskName" /tr "command" /sc daily
        Extract system information remotely: psexec \\target systeminfo > host_info.txt
        Map network drives for file operations: psexec \\target net use Z: \\server\share /persistent:yes
        Execute commands with alternate credentials file: psexec @credentials.txt -h cmd.exe
        Run commands silently without console output: psexec \\target -d -h command.exe
        Modify registry settings remotely: psexec \\target reg add "HKLM\Software\Example" /v "Value" /t REG_SZ /d "Data"
        Execute WMI queries through PsExec: psexec \\target wmic process list
        Deploy and configure firewall rules: psexec \\target netsh advfirewall firewall add rule
        Run scripts with redirected output: psexec \\target script.bat > output.log 2>&1
        Execute commands through named pipes: psexec \\target -r pipename cmd.exe
        Bypass UAC using PsExec: psexec -i -d -h \\target "cmd /c whoami /groups"
        Execute commands with specific process priority: psexec \\target -low -d command.exe
        Run commands with alternative service name: psexec \\target -r altservice -s cmd
        Perform remote system shutdown/restart: psexec \\target shutdown /r /t 0
        Export and collect event logs: psexec \\target wevtutil epl System sys.evtx
        Modify local group membership: psexec \\target net localgroup administrators username /add
        Execute commands with specific session ID: psexec \\target -i 1 cmd.exe
        Deploy and start performance monitoring: psexec \\target perfmon /start
        Clear system logs remotely: psexec \\target wevtutil cl System
        Create remote process dump: psexec \\target procdump -ma process.exe dump.dmp
        Enumerate network shares remotely: psexec \\target net share > shares.txt
        Create and modify user accounts: psexec \\target net user newuser password /add
        Execute commands with specific timeout: psexec \\target -n 30 long-running-script.bat
        Deploy and start packet capture: psexec \\target netsh trace start capture=yes
        Modify boot configuration: psexec \\target bcdedit /set {default} bootstatuspolicy ignoreallfailures
        Execute commands with specific working directory: psexec \\target -w c:\temp cmd.exe
        Install Windows updates remotely: psexec \\target wusa.exe update.msu /quiet
        Configure remote desktop settings: psexec \\target reg add "HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Terminal Server" /v fDenyTSConnections /t REG_DWORD /d 0 /f
        Export security policy settings: psexec \\target secedit /export /cfg security.cfg
        Modify service recovery options: psexec \\target sc failure service_name reset= 0 actions= restart/60000/restart/60000/restart/60000
