    Security Testing Frameworks - Comprehensive platforms for security assessment
      Metasploit Framework - Modular penetration testing platform with exploit development and vulnerability verification capabilities
        Initial setup procedure: Install and configure Metasploit Framework, set up PostgreSQL database, update exploit modules, and configure workspace
        Remote exploitation procedure: Select exploit module, configure target parameters, set payload options (reverse shell/meterpreter), and execute exploit
        Payload generation and delivery: Create custom payloads using msfvenom, encode/encrypt to bypass AV, deliver through various channels (web, email, USB)
        Local privilege escalation: Use post-exploitation modules to identify system vulnerabilities, exploit local weaknesses, and elevate privileges
        Network enumeration and lateral movement: Use auxiliary scanners for host discovery, port scanning, and service enumeration, then pivot to other systems
        Persistence establishment: Install backdoors, create scheduled tasks, modify registry keys, and deploy persistent agents using post modules
        Credential harvesting: Dump password hashes, extract cached credentials, and perform pass-the-hash attacks using built-in modules
        Data exfiltration: Identify and collect sensitive data, compress/encrypt files, and transfer through established C2 channels
        Resource script automation: Create custom resource scripts to automate common attack sequences and post-exploitation tasks
        C2 infrastructure setup: Configure handlers, establish multi-handler listeners, and manage multiple sessions across compromised hosts
        Custom module development: Write new exploit modules in Ruby, create custom auxiliary modules, and integrate with existing framework
        Antivirus evasion: Use encoders, encryptors, and packers to modify payload signatures, implement custom shellcode, and bypass detection
        Web application testing: Use auxiliary modules for web crawling, vulnerability scanning, and exploitation of common web vulnerabilities
