        Network scanning using custom TCP/IP packets: Craft TCP SYN packets for stealth port scanning, customize packet headers, and analyze responses
        DNS reconnaissance: Create custom DNS queries to enumerate domains, perform DNS tunneling, and test for zone transfer vulnerabilities
        ARP cache poisoning: Forge ARP packets to intercept network traffic between hosts, enabling man-in-the-middle attacks
        Custom protocol fuzzing: Generate malformed packets to test protocol implementations and discover vulnerabilities
        Network traffic manipulation: Intercept, modify, and inject packets into existing network connections
        Wireless network attacks: Create deauthentication frames, probe requests, and beacon frames for WiFi testing
        DHCP starvation: Generate multiple DHCP requests with different MAC addresses to exhaust DHCP server pool
        VLAN hopping: Craft double-tagged 802.1Q packets to bypass VLAN segmentation
        Protocol-specific exploits: Create custom packets for exploiting known vulnerabilities in various protocols (ICMP, TCP, UDP)
        Covert channel creation: Establish hidden communication channels using custom protocol implementations
        Packet sniffing and analysis: Capture network traffic, filter specific protocols, and analyze packet contents for sensitive information
        TCP session hijacking: Craft packets to take over existing TCP sessions by predicting sequence numbers
        IP spoofing attacks: Generate packets with forged source IP addresses to bypass security controls or conduct reflection attacks
        ICMP tunneling: Create covert channels using custom ICMP packets for data exfiltration
        MAC flooding: Send numerous packets with different source MAC addresses to overflow switch CAM tables
        Protocol reverse engineering: Capture and analyze unknown protocols to understand their structure and behavior
        Network baseline profiling: Capture and analyze normal traffic patterns to blend malicious activities
        Custom packet replay: Record and replay modified packet sequences for testing or exploitation
        BGP hijacking simulation: Craft BGP packets to test routing infrastructure security
        Layer 2 protocol attacks: Exploit STP, CDP, or other layer 2 protocols through custom packet crafting
        Custom IDS/IPS evasion: Fragment packets and manipulate TCP/IP headers to bypass network security controls
        IPv6-based attacks: Craft malicious IPv6 packets for networks with dual-stack implementations
        VoIP protocol manipulation: Create custom SIP and RTP packets for VoIP infrastructure testing
        Network QoS manipulation: Craft packets with specific DSCP values to abuse QoS mechanisms
        Custom packet-based C2: Implement command and control channels using custom protocol fields
        SSL/TLS protocol testing: Craft custom handshake messages and test cipher implementations
        Network timing attacks: Create precisely timed packet sequences for side-channel attacks
        Protocol mutation: Modify standard protocols to create hybrid packets that bypass filtering
        Raw socket manipulation: Bypass OS network stack restrictions using raw socket implementations
        Custom network fingerprinting: Develop unique packet sequences for target OS/service identification
        Industrial protocol testing: Craft custom Modbus, DNP3, or other ICS protocol packets for testing industrial networks
        IoT protocol exploitation: Generate custom MQTT, CoAP, or other IoT protocol packets for device testing
        Custom network stress testing: Create high-volume packet streams with specific patterns to test network resilience
        Network topology mapping: Use custom packet sequences to discover and map network relationships
        Protocol state manipulation: Exploit protocol state machines through carefully crafted packet sequences
        Multicast protocol abuse: Manipulate multicast protocol packets for amplification attacks
        Network timing synchronization attacks: Manipulate NTP or PTP packets to disrupt time synchronization
        SDN protocol testing: Craft OpenFlow or other SDN protocol packets to test network programmability
