        Custom compression configuration: Adjust AVML compression settings to balance between acquisition speed and storage requirements
        Automated memory collection: Set up scheduled tasks to periodically capture memory using AVML for baseline analysis
        Multi-format export: Configure AVML output for compatibility with multiple analysis platforms (Volatility, Rekall) through format conversion
        Error recovery procedure: Implement fallback mechanisms for handling interrupted acquisitions or system resource constraints
        Memory acquisition verification: Use AVML's built-in integrity checking features to validate captured memory dumps
        Large system optimization: Configure AVML for efficient memory acquisition on systems with large RAM (>128GB)
        Kernel module compatibility: Adjust AVML settings to handle systems with custom or non-standard kernel modules
