      WinPmem - Open source memory acquisition tool
        Execute WinPmem with basic memory capture: winpmem.exe memory.raw
        Use compression to reduce dump size: winpmem.exe -c memory.zip
        Capture memory to remote location: winpmem.exe \\remote\share\memory.raw
        Extract kernel drivers using /driver option: winpmem.exe /driver driver.sys
        Perform memory acquisition with specific compression level: winpmem.exe -c 1 memory.zip
        Use alternate output formats (crashdump): winpmem.exe --format crashdump memory.dmp
        Acquire memory with write mode enabled: winpmem.exe -w memory.raw
        Extract pagefile along with memory: winpmem.exe --pagefile memory.raw
        Use low priority mode for stealth: winpmem.exe -l memory.raw
        Capture memory with metadata logging: winpmem.exe --logfile log.txt memory.raw
        Specify memory ranges for selective capture: winpmem.exe -r 0x0000,0xFFFF memory.raw
        Use double buffering for faster acquisition: winpmem.exe --buffer 2 memory.raw
        Verify captured memory integrity: winpmem.exe --verify memory.raw
        Generate acquisition metadata in JSON format: winpmem.exe --json metadata.json memory.raw
        Perform dry run to estimate required space: winpmem.exe --dry-run
        Capture with specific sector size: winpmem.exe --sector-size 4096 memory.raw
        Use kernel mode acquisition method: winpmem.exe --mode kernel memory.raw
        Enable verbose output for debugging: winpmem.exe -v memory.raw
        Integrate with volatility for immediate analysis: winpmem.exe --format volatility memory.raw
        Execute with specific process priority: winpmem.exe --priority high memory.raw
        Create memory dump with system state information: winpmem.exe --include-state memory.raw
        Handle large memory systems with splitting: winpmem.exe --split-size 2G memory.raw
        Use fallback acquisition method on failure: winpmem.exe --fallback memory.raw
        Execute with specific timestamp preservation: winpmem.exe --preserve-timestamps memory.raw
        Implement memory capture with retry mechanism: winpmem.exe --retry-count 3 memory.raw
        Perform acquisition with system cache bypass: winpmem.exe --nocache memory.raw
        Create acquisition log with system details: winpmem.exe --sysinfo memory.raw
        Use specific memory map method: winpmem.exe --map-type physical memory.raw
