    Exploitation Frameworks - Platforms specifically designed for exploit development and deployment
      Metasploit Framework - Modular penetration testing platform with extensive exploit, payload, and post-exploitation capabilities
        Basic MSF Deployment: Install and configure Metasploit Framework, set up PostgreSQL database, update exploit database, configure workspace, and establish proper networking settings
        Exploit Development Workflow: Research target vulnerabilities, select or develop appropriate exploit modules, configure exploit parameters, test in lab environment, and prepare for deployment
        Handler and Payload Generation: Configure multi-handler listeners, generate various payload types (staged/stageless), encode payloads to evade detection, create custom shellcode, and establish C2 channels
        Automated Target Discovery: Use auxiliary modules for port scanning, service enumeration, vulnerability assessment, and credential harvesting against target networks
        Web Application Exploitation: Deploy web-based exploits, conduct SQL injection attacks, exploit file upload vulnerabilities, and leverage web application assessment modules
        Post-Exploitation Operations: Execute privilege escalation modules, harvest credentials, establish persistence, conduct lateral movement, and maintain access using Meterpreter sessions
        Network Infrastructure Attacks: Exploit network services, conduct SMB relay attacks, leverage protocol-specific vulnerabilities, and compromise network devices
        Data Collection and Exfiltration: Gather system information, extract sensitive files, capture screenshots, record keystrokes, and exfiltrate data through established channels
        Automation and Scripting: Develop custom resource scripts, automate exploitation workflows, create macro-based payloads, and build automated attack chains
        Evasion Techniques: Implement payload encoding, use process injection, employ anti-forensics methods, and bypass security controls using built-in evasion modules
        Social Engineering Attacks: Configure Social Engineering Toolkit (SET) integration, create phishing campaigns, generate malicious documents, and deploy client-side attacks
        Pivoting Operations: Set up pivot listeners, route traffic through compromised hosts, deploy SOCKS proxies, and chain multiple sessions for network access
        Custom Module Development: Create custom auxiliary, exploit, and post modules using Ruby, integrate external tools, and develop new payloads for specific targets
        Credential Attack Campaigns: Deploy password bruteforce modules, conduct pass-the-hash attacks, exploit authentication mechanisms, and leverage gathered credentials
        Defense Evasion Framework: Implement in-memory execution, use DLL injection techniques, bypass AMSI, and leverage process hollowing modules
        Database Operations: Manage multiple workspaces, document findings, export reports, and maintain operational security through proper database handling
        Active Directory Exploitation: Deploy DCSync attacks, golden ticket generation, domain enumeration, and leverage Active Directory-specific modules
        Hardware and IoT Exploitation: Use specialized modules for embedded systems, exploit firmware vulnerabilities, and target IoT devices
        Mobile Device Attacks: Deploy Android/iOS-specific exploits, generate mobile payloads, and exploit mobile device vulnerabilities
        Cloud Infrastructure Attacks: Exploit cloud service misconfigurations, deploy cloud-specific modules, and target containerized environments
        Protocol-Specific Exploitation: Target industrial protocols (Modbus, S7, DNP3), exploit VoIP systems, and leverage specialized protocol fuzzers
        Wireless Network Attacks: Deploy wireless assessment modules, exploit WPA/WPA2 vulnerabilities, conduct evil twin attacks, and target Bluetooth devices
        Virtualization Infrastructure Attacks: Target hypervisors, exploit container escapes, attack management interfaces, and compromise virtual machines
        Integration with C2 Frameworks: Configure staging for Empire/Covenant payloads, integrate with Cobalt Strike beacons, and chain with other C2 frameworks
        Advanced Persistence Techniques: Implement bootkit deployment, establish registry-free persistence, create WMI event consumers, and leverage COM hijacking
        Anti-Forensics Operations: Implement secure file deletion, manipulate timestamps, clear logs, and deploy anti-memory forensics techniques
        Supply Chain Attack Simulation: Exploit software distribution mechanisms, compromise update channels, and target development tools
        SCADA/ICS Targeting: Deploy industrial control system exploits, target PLCs, and exploit SCADA protocols
        Specialized Database Attacks: Target NoSQL databases, exploit specific database engines, and leverage database-specific vulnerabilities
        Kernel Exploitation: Deploy kernel-level payloads, exploit driver vulnerabilities, and implement rootkit functionality
        Advanced AV Evasion: Implement runtime API unhooking, use shellcode staging techniques, deploy custom encoders, and utilize advanced obfuscation methods
        Compliance Testing Operations: Execute PCI-DSS assessment modules, HIPAA compliance checks, and regulatory requirement validation tests
        Cross-Platform Attack Chains: Coordinate attacks across Windows/Linux/macOS systems, leverage multi-platform payloads, and exploit cross-platform vulnerabilities
        Custom Malware Integration: Package custom malware with MSF payloads, implement fileless malware deployment, and create hybrid attack chains
        Advanced Memory Manipulation: Implement direct syscall techniques, use reflective DLL injection, and deploy advanced process injection methods
        Hardware Security Bypass: Exploit firmware vulnerabilities, deploy Intel ME attacks, and target hardware security modules
        Network Protocol Tunneling: Implement custom protocol tunneling, create covert channels, and leverage protocol-specific data exfiltration
        Advanced Lateral Movement: Deploy Pass-the-Ticket attacks, leverage shadow copy exploitation, and implement advanced domain persistence
        Air-Gapped Network Attacks: Develop specialized data exfiltration techniques, implement acoustic/electromagnetic covert channels, and exploit isolated systems
        Distributed Attack Orchestration: Coordinate multiple MSF instances, implement distributed scanning, and manage large-scale exploitation campaigns
