      SET (Social Engineer Toolkit) - Framework specifically designed for social engineering attacks
        Website cloning attack: Clone legitimate websites using SET's web attack vector, customize the cloned site for credential harvesting, deploy on local/remote server, and collect submitted credentials
        Spear-phishing campaign: Generate malicious email templates, embed payload using SET's spear-phishing attack vector, customize sender information, and track email opens/clicks
        QRCode attack: Create malicious QR codes using SET's QRCode generator, embed links to credential harvesting pages, and deploy in physical locations or via email
        Wireless access point attack: Create rogue wireless access points using SET's wireless attack vector, set up captive portals for credential harvesting, and intercept network traffic
        PowerShell attack vector: Generate PowerShell-based payloads, encode to bypass detection, and deliver through social engineering scenarios
        Java applet attack: Create malicious Java applets using SET's web attack vector, sign with stolen/self-signed certificates, and deploy through compromised websites
        SMS spoofing campaign: Use SET's SMS spoofing capabilities to send targeted text messages, include malicious links, and harvest credentials through mobile phishing
        Credential harvester: Deploy SET's credential harvester, customize landing pages for specific organizations, and collect/exfiltrate captured credentials
        Mass mailer attack: Configure SET's mass mailer, import target lists, customize templates with social engineering lures, and track campaign effectiveness
        Tabnabbing attack: Set up tab nabbing attacks using SET's web attack vector, wait for user inactivity, and redirect to credential harvesting pages
        USB/DVD AutoRun attack: Create autorun malware using SET's infectious media generator, configure payload execution, and deploy via physical media distribution
        Multi-Attack Web Method: Combine multiple web attack vectors (Java applet, credential harvester, metasploit browser exploits) into a single unified attack
        Arduino-based attack: Program Arduino devices using SET's teensy attack vector, create HID exploits, and deploy through physical access
        Infectious PDF operation: Generate malicious PDF documents with embedded payloads, customize templates, and distribute through social engineering
        Custom EXE payload creation: Use SET's payload generator to create custom executable files, encode/encrypt for AV evasion, and deploy via social engineering
        Web Jacking attack: Deploy SET's web jacking module, clone legitimate sites, inject malicious iframes, and capture user interactions
        Third-party web templates: Import and customize third-party website templates, modify for specific target organizations, deploy credential harvesters
        DNS spoofing campaign: Configure SET's DNS spoofing capabilities, redirect target traffic to malicious sites, capture credentials and session data
        SET API integration: Configure SET's API for automated attacks, integrate with custom tools, and orchestrate multiple attack vectors programmatically
        Custom payload encoding: Use SET's payload encoding options, implement multiple encoding layers, bypass AV detection through customized encoders
        Site cloner with 2FA bypass: Deploy advanced web cloning with two-factor authentication interception, relay captured codes in real-time
        Remote template update: Configure SET to pull updated templates from remote repositories, maintain fresh social engineering scenarios, automate template management
