      Nikto - Web server scanner for dangerous files/CGIs
        Basic vulnerability scanning: Execute Nikto with default options against target web server (-h target_host) to identify common vulnerabilities and misconfigurations
        Comprehensive scan with SSL: Perform full scan of HTTPS-enabled web servers using -ssl option and custom ports (-p port) to identify SSL-related vulnerabilities
        Stealth scanning: Configure scan with reduced noise (-Display V) and tuning options (-Tuning x) to avoid detection, adjust request timing (-delay x)
        Custom authentication: Scan authenticated areas using credential options (-id username:password) and cookie handling (-Cookie value) to test protected sections
        Targeted scanning: Focus on specific vulnerability types or tests using tuning options (-Tuning 123) and plugins (-Plugins tests)
        Multiple host scanning: Scan multiple targets using host list file (-h host.txt) with parallel scanning (-mutiple x) for efficiency
        Custom reporting: Generate detailed reports in various formats (-Format htm,csv,xml) and save output (-output file) for analysis
        Proxy usage: Configure scanning through proxy servers (-proxy host:port) for anonymity or accessing restricted targets
        Custom database updates: Update and manage Nikto's vulnerability database (nikto -update) to include latest security checks
        Plugin development: Create custom test plugins (.plugin files) to extend scanning capabilities for specific vulnerabilities
        Web server version fingerprinting: Use Nikto's server fingerprinting capabilities (-vhost) to identify server type, version, and potential version-specific vulnerabilities
        Virtual host scanning: Configure scanning for virtual hosts and subdomains (-vhost) with custom hostname headers
        Custom HTTP methods: Test non-standard HTTP methods (-Option METHOD) to identify unusual server configurations
        Integration with Metasploit: Configure Nikto output for direct import into Metasploit (-Format msf) for further exploitation
        Rate limiting bypass: Implement techniques to bypass server-side rate limiting using custom headers and request delays
        CGI scanning optimization: Focus on CGI script enumeration and testing with specific tuning options (-Tuning 0)
        Custom payload testing: Define and test custom payloads against discovered endpoints using mutation options
        Error page analysis: Configure detailed error page analysis (-404code) to identify information disclosure
        Session handling: Implement advanced session management with custom tokens and cookies for authenticated scans
        Compliance checking: Perform specific compliance-related checks (PCI, HIPAA) using appropriate tuning and plugins
        API endpoint scanning: Configure Nikto for testing REST API endpoints with custom headers and authentication tokens
        WAF detection and evasion: Implement techniques to detect and bypass Web Application Firewall protections using custom headers and request patterns
        Automated scanning pipeline: Integrate Nikto into CI/CD pipelines using automation scripts and custom triggers
        Database backend testing: Focus scanning on identifying database exposure and injection points using specific tuning options
        SSL/TLS configuration testing: Detailed SSL/TLS security configuration checking with enhanced SSL options (-ssl -sslcheck)
        Custom dictionary attacks: Implement custom wordlists and dictionaries for targeted directory and file enumeration
        Docker container scanning: Configure Nikto for scanning containerized web applications with specific considerations
        Cloud platform scanning: Adapt scanning parameters for cloud-hosted applications (AWS, Azure, GCP) with appropriate rate limiting
        Legacy system scanning: Modify scanning parameters for testing older web servers and applications with legacy protocols
        Scheduled scanning: Implement automated periodic scanning with custom intervals and differential reporting
