        Perform recursive directory scanning with depth control (e.g., `gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt -r -d 3`)
        Use pattern matching and status code filtering (e.g., `gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt -b 403,404`)
        Employ custom HTTP headers for bypass attempts (e.g., `gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt -H 'User-Agent: CustomBot'`)
        Configure proxy settings for anonymous scanning (e.g., `gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt --proxy socks5://127.0.0.1:9050`)
        Utilize wildcard DNS enumeration (e.g., `gobuster dns -d target.com -w wordlist.txt --wildcard`)
        Implement custom output formatting and reporting (e.g., `gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt -o output.txt -f`)
        Perform authenticated scanning using basic auth (e.g., `gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt -U username -P password`)
        Use custom DNS resolvers for enumeration (e.g., `gobuster dns -d target.com -w wordlist.txt -r 8.8.8.8`)
        Implement rate limiting to avoid detection (e.g., `gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt --delay 100ms`)
        Utilize fuzzing mode for parameter discovery (e.g., `gobuster fuzz -u http://target.com/FUZZ -w wordlist.txt`)
        Combine with pattern matching for sensitive file discovery (e.g., `gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt -x conf,config,bak,backup,swp,old,db,sql`)
        Execute with custom timeout settings (e.g., `gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt --timeout 30s`)
        Perform TLS configuration scanning (e.g., `gobuster dir -u https://target.com -w wordlist.txt -k --tls-skip-verify`)
        Use custom string matching for content discovery (e.g., `gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt -s "admin panel"`)
        Chain with wget for automatic content retrieval (e.g., `gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt | grep "Status: 200" | cut -d " " -f1 | xargs -I% wget http://target.com/%`)
        Use custom wordlist generation with CeWL integration (e.g., `cewl http://target.com -m 5 -w custom_wordlist.txt && gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w custom_wordlist.txt`)
        Implement URL encoding for special character handling (e.g., `gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt --url-encode`)
        Perform distributed scanning across multiple IPs (e.g., `gobuster dns -d target.com -w wordlist.txt -i /path/to/ip_list.txt`)
        Use expanded mode for detailed response analysis (e.g., `gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt -e --expanded`)
        Conduct case-insensitive scanning for Windows targets (e.g., `gobuster dir -u http://target.com -w wordlist.txt --case-insensitive`)
