      Hakrawler - Web crawler for gathering endpoints
        Basic endpoint discovery: Install Hakrawler via Go, run against target domain with 'hakrawler -url https://target.com', collect all discovered endpoints
        Recursive crawling: Execute with depth parameter (-depth 3) to discover nested endpoints and perform thorough mapping of application structure
        JavaScript file analysis: Use with -js flag to extract endpoints from JavaScript files and identify potential API endpoints
        Authenticated crawling: Configure with custom headers (-h "Cookie: session=xyz") to crawl authenticated sections of applications
        Subdomain enumeration: Combine with subfinder/amass output to crawl multiple subdomains, pipe results through hakrawler
        Custom regex patterns: Deploy with -pattern flag to search for specific patterns in responses (API keys, tokens, sensitive endpoints)
        Output filtering: Use with grep/sed to filter and categorize discovered endpoints based on patterns (/api/, /admin/, etc.)
        Scope-based crawling: Configure with -scope flag to limit crawling to specific domain patterns and avoid out-of-scope requests
        Sitemap discovery: Target /sitemap.xml first, then use discovered URLs as input for deeper crawling
        Rate-limited crawling: Use -delay parameter to avoid detection and respect server limitations
        Parallel crawling: Use multiple instances with different starting points to speed up discovery, combine results using sort/uniq
        WAF evasion: Modify user-agent (-h "User-Agent: custom"), rotate IPs, and adjust timing to bypass security controls
        Parameter discovery: Extract and analyze URL parameters from crawled endpoints for potential injection points
        API endpoint collection: Focus crawling on API documentation pages (/swagger, /api-docs) to map API structure
        File type targeting: Use grep to filter discovered endpoints by file extensions (.php, .asp, .jsp) for targeted testing
        Historical endpoint discovery: Combine with Wayback Machine data to discover deprecated but still accessible endpoints
        Custom wordlist generation: Process crawled endpoints to create application-specific wordlists for further testing
        Error page analysis: Collect and analyze error responses for information disclosure and potential vulnerabilities
        Backend service discovery: Identify patterns in URLs that reveal internal service names or architectures
        Content type mapping: Categorize endpoints by content-type headers to identify different application components
        CI/CD integration: Automate Hakrawler scanning in CI/CD pipelines to continuously monitor endpoint changes
        GraphQL discovery: Target specific paths (/graphql, /graphiql) to enumerate GraphQL endpoints and query structures
        Load balancer detection: Analyze response headers of crawled endpoints to identify load balancing patterns
        WebSocket endpoint discovery: Focus on WebSocket endpoints (ws://, wss://) for real-time communication channels
        Cloud storage discovery: Extract and validate URLs pointing to cloud storage (S3 buckets, Azure blobs) from responses
        Version control exposure: Identify exposed version control directories (.git, .svn) during crawling
        Database connection string discovery: Search for exposed database connection strings in JavaScript files
