      Feroxbuster - Fast content discovery tool
        Basic directory enumeration using default wordlist and recursive scanning with command: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com -w /path/to/wordlist`
        Scan multiple domains simultaneously using target file: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com --stdin < domains.txt`
        Filter responses by status codes to identify specific server behaviors: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com --status-codes 200,301,302,403`
        Customize scan depth and parallelism: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com -d 3 --threads 100`
        Extract and scan discovered links: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com --extract-links`
        Target specific file extensions: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com -x php,asp,html,js`
        Authenticate scanning with headers: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com -H "Authorization: Bearer token"`
        Save scan results in multiple formats: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com --json --output results.json`
        Proxy requests through Burp Suite: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com --proxy http://127.0.0.1:8080`
        Scan with custom timeout and rate limiting: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com --timeout 7 --rate-limit 50`
        Silent mode scanning with minimal output: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com -q --silent`
        Scan with custom wordlist and auto-tune settings: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com -w custom.txt --auto-tune`
        Filter by response size to identify interesting content: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com --filter-size 1234`
        Add random User-Agent headers: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com --random-agent`
        Scan with specific methods: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com -m GET,POST,PUT`
        Ignore specific word patterns: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com --dont-scan "logout|admin|config"`
        Resume previous scan from state file: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com --resume-from state.save`
        Collect all responses in directory: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com --collect-responses`
        Scan with specific extensions and backups: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com -x php,bak,old,backup`
        Follow redirects with depth control: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com --redirects --depth 2`
        Insecure SSL scanning: `feroxbuster -u https://target.com -k --insecure`
        Scan with custom DNS resolution: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com --add-header "Host: internal.target.com"`
        Time-based filtering to identify slow endpoints: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com --filter-time 3000`
        Parallel scanning with URL rewriting: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com --url-rewriting`
        Smart scan with content type filtering: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com --filter-similar-to 0.95`
        Extract parameters from discovered endpoints: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com --extract-links --collect-queries`
        Scan with specific encoding: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com --url-encode`
        Customize scan with regex filters: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com --regex-filter "admin|login"`
        Nested directory depth scanning: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com --depth 4 --scan-limit 50000`
        Save scan progress periodically: `feroxbuster -u http://target.com --save-state progress.state --auto-save`
