      HashCat - Advanced password recovery and cracking tool
        Dictionary attack with custom rules: Configure HashCat to use wordlists (e.g., rockyou.txt) with custom rule sets (e.g., best64.rule) to generate password variations, specify hash type (-m), and utilize GPU acceleration for faster cracking
        Brute force attack using mask patterns: Set up character sets and patterns (e.g., ?d?d?d?d?d?d for 6-digit PINs) to systematically test all possible combinations for specific password formats
        Hybrid attack combining wordlists and masks: Combine dictionary words with appended/prepended numbers or special characters using hybrid attack modes (-a 6 or -a 7) to crack complex passwords
        NTLM hash cracking: Extract NTLM hashes from Windows SAM database or NTDS.dit, convert to HashCat format, and perform cracking using appropriate hash mode (-m 1000)
        WPA/WPA2 handshake cracking: Convert captured handshake to HCCAPX format, specify wireless hash mode (-m 2500), and use appropriate wordlist or mask attack
        Distributed cracking setup: Configure HashCat to run across multiple GPU-enabled systems using the --backend-devices parameter and custom scripts for workload distribution
        Rainbow table attack: Generate or obtain pre-computed rainbow tables, configure HashCat for table-based attacks, and perform lookups against captured hashes
        Rule-based mutation attack: Create custom rule sets to generate password variations based on known patterns, corporate naming conventions, or target-specific information
        Combinator attack: Combine multiple wordlists to create compound passwords using HashCat's built-in combinator attack mode (-a 1)
        Optimized GPU tuning: Configure workload optimization parameters (-w), kernel optimization, and temperature management for maximum cracking performance
        Linux shadow file cracking: Extract hashes from /etc/shadow, identify hash type (SHA-512, SHA-256, etc.), convert to HashCat format, and execute cracking with appropriate mode (-m 1800 for SHA-512crypt)
        Memory-based attack optimization: Configure session management, restore/resume capabilities, and potfile usage for handling large hash sets efficiently
        Office document password recovery: Convert protected Office documents to HashCat format using office2john, select appropriate hash mode (-m 9400 for Office 2007), and perform cracking
        PDF password cracking: Extract PDF hash using pdf2john, configure appropriate hash mode (-m 10500 for PDF 1.7), and execute cracking with targeted wordlists
        Database hash cracking: Process MySQL, PostgreSQL, or Oracle database password hashes with specific modes (e.g., -m 300 for MySQL4.1/MySQL5)
        Blockchain wallet recovery: Configure HashCat for cryptocurrency wallet password recovery using specific modes for Bitcoin, Ethereum, or other blockchain wallets
        Custom charset attacks: Define and use custom character sets (--custom-charset) for targeting organization-specific password policies or known patterns
        Markov-chain attack: Implement Markov-chain based password generation using HashCat's built-in Markov mode for more efficient password guessing
        Multi-hash attack optimization: Configure HashCat for simultaneously cracking multiple hash types using optimized workload distribution and hash-type groups
        Password analysis and reporting: Use HashCat's output for statistical analysis, pattern recognition, and compliance reporting of cracked passwords
        macOS keychain cracking: Extract keychain hashes using chainbreaker, convert to HashCat format, and execute cracking with appropriate hash mode (-m 23100)
        Zip/Archive password recovery: Process encrypted archives (ZIP, RAR, 7z) using zip2john/rar2john, select appropriate hash mode (-m 13600 for WinZip), and perform cracking
        Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) hash cracking: Extract and crack RDP credentials from Windows systems using appropriate hash modes and optimized wordlists
        Kerberos ticket cracking: Process Kerberos TGS-REP tickets (-m 13100) and AS-REP roasting hashes (-m 18200) for Active Directory credential recovery
        SSH private key passphrase cracking: Convert SSH private keys to HashCat format using ssh2john, select appropriate mode, and execute cracking
        LUKS volume password recovery: Extract LUKS header information, configure appropriate hash mode (-m 14600), and perform cryptographic attack
        Integration with automated tools: Configure HashCat for automated operation with custom scripts, APIs, or penetration testing frameworks
        Token/Cookie session cracking: Process web application session tokens or cookies using appropriate modes and custom rule sets
        Hardware security module (HSM) backup key recovery: Configure specialized attacks for encrypted HSM backup files using appropriate modes
        Two-factor authentication backup code cracking: Process 2FA backup codes using pattern-based attacks and specialized masks
