      Kubeaudit - Kubernetes security auditing tool
        Scan Kubernetes clusters for security issues using all available auditors: `kubeaudit all -f /path/to/manifest.yaml`
        Identify containers running with root privileges using: `kubeaudit nonroot`
        Check for privileged container settings with: `kubeaudit privileged`
        Audit network policies and exposed services using: `kubeaudit network`
        Detect missing resource limits using: `kubeaudit limits`
        Scan for containers with dangerous capabilities enabled: `kubeaudit caps`
        Check for exposed service accounts and RBAC misconfigurations: `kubeaudit automountServiceAccountToken`
        Identify containers running with host-level access: `kubeaudit hostns`
        Audit security context configurations using: `kubeaudit securitycontext`
        Generate comprehensive JSON reports for further analysis: `kubeaudit all -f /path/to/manifest.yaml -o json`
        Integrate Kubeaudit into CI/CD pipeline: `kubeaudit all -f ${MANIFEST_PATH} --exit-code 2`
        Create custom audit rules using MutatingWebhookConfiguration: `kubeaudit all --custom-audit-path /path/to/custom/rules.yaml`
        Perform selective auditing with multiple specific auditors: `kubeaudit -k ~/.kube/config securitycontext privileged nonroot`
        Execute namespace-specific security audits: `kubeaudit all -n target-namespace`
        Audit specific Kubernetes resources: `kubeaudit all --kinds Pod,Deployment,StatefulSet`
        Generate machine-readable output for automated analysis: `kubeaudit all --format junit`
        Perform security audits against multiple contexts: `kubeaudit all --context-name prod-cluster`
        Use ignore patterns to bypass specific security checks: `kubeaudit all --ignore-failures-for-rules privileged,automountServiceAccountToken`
        Audit historical deployments using manifest files from version control: `kubeaudit all -f ./k8s-manifests/*`
        Generate HTML security reports for stakeholder review: `kubeaudit all --format html > report.html`
